  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hari Shankar Singh @ Hari Shankar Prasad vs The State Of Jharkhand ... Opposite ... on 27 February, 2024 Author: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi Bench: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi 1 Cr.M.P. No. 2009 of 2018 In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr.M.P. No. 2009 of 2018 1.Hari Shankar Singh @ Hari Shankar Prasad 2.Dharmendra Kumar @ Dharmendra Kumar Singh 3.Kesaw Singh @ Keshaw @ Keswav Singh... Petitioners -Versus- The State of Jharkhand ... Opposite Party ----- Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi ----- For the Petitioner : Mr. Arvind Kumar Choudhary, Advocate For the Opposite Party-State : Mr. Shashi Kumar Verma, Advocate ----- 5/27.02.2024.",
    "facts": "On 14.8.2015 Keshaw Singh and Hari Shankar Singh @ Hari Shankar Prasad vs The State Of Jharkhand ... Opposite ... on 27 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/192656336/ 1",
    "arguments": "He submits that procedure for registration of the case under section 42 of the Act of 2006 is concerned that has not been followed and the FIR is registered by Officer incharge of Muri Railway Station and the case is against the provision of statute which is a special Act. He further submits that the designated officer appointed under section 36 of the Act can scrutinize the report of analyst and decide whether the prosecution can be lodged and he can send the said recommendation within specified period of time for sanctioning such prosecution and after sanction by the competent authority the case can be lodged. 5. Learned counsel for the State opposed the prayer on the ground that case is made out and rightly the case has been lodged."
  },
